    {
      "id": "8XkgA1GlGUz1ZnKFnNtsH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 313.515625,
      "y": 655.48828125,
      "width": 776.8372802734375,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1103900954,
      "version": 267,
      "versionNonce": 1771703366,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787326721917,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Core Entities\n\n1) Logger: The orchestrator. Holds the immutable list of destinations, exposes\nlog() and convenience methods, captures per-call data (timestamp, thread\nname) and builds the LogRecord.\n\n2) Destionation: One configured output target. Owns its minimum level\nthreshold, holds a reference to its formatter, and serializes the filter-format-\nwrite workflow. Where the per-destination lock will live.\n\n3) Formatter: An interface for serializing a LogRecord to a string. Two\nimplementations exist (plain text and JSON), and new formats become new\nimplementations without touching anything else.\n\n4) LogRecord: An immutable value object carrying the four pieces of per-call\ndata (timestamp, level, message, thread name). Created in Logger.log(),\nconsumed by every destination.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Core Entities\n\n1) Logger: The orchestrator. Holds the immutable list of destinations, exposes log() and convenience methods, captures per-call data (timestamp, thread name) and builds the LogRecord.\n\n2) Destionation: One configured output target. Owns its minimum level threshold, holds a reference to its formatter, and serializes the filter-format-write workflow. Where the per-destination lock will live.\n\n3) Formatter: An interface for serializing a LogRecord to a string. Two implementations exist (plain text and JSON), and new formats become new implementations without touching anything else.\n\n4) LogRecord: An immutable value object carrying the four pieces of per-call data (timestamp, level, message, thread name). Created in Logger.log(), consumed by every destination.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "F18SG2mryueL1paPGzOU7",
