      "text": "2) How to support hierrachial named logger",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2) How to support hierrachial named logger",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "DfIIu8CU0X-gtoVYo3pde",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1148,
      "y": 780.5,
      "width": 940.8249511718748,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5Q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 626996038,
      "version": 129,
      "versionNonce": 1869214618,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787327698227,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"com.app.service.payments\"), and the returned logger inherits\nconfiguration from its parent in the dotted-name tree ==> add a name field and a parent\npointer to Logger, and put a LoggerFactory in front of construction. The factory keeps a\nregistry keyed by name, looks up the parent from the dotted prefix, and falls back to the root\nwhen none exists. Effective level and effective destinations walk the parent chain when they're\nnot set on the logger itself.\n\n- Caching: cache the effective level on each Logger and invalidate it when configuration changes,\ninstead of walking the parent chain on every call.\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"com.app.service.payments\"), and the returned logger inherits configuration from its parent in the dotted-name tree ==> add a name field and a parent pointer to Logger, and put a LoggerFactory in front of construction. The factory keeps a registry keyed by name, looks up the parent from the dotted prefix, and falls back to the root when none exists. Effective level and effective destinations walk the parent chain when they're not set on the logger itself.\n\n- Caching: cache the effective level on each Logger and invalidate it when configuration changes, instead of walking the parent chain on every call.\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
