      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787327949533,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) Ingest tier: Authenticates agents, validates payloads, and enforces per-tenant quotas\nbefore anything is accepted.\n2) Kafka buffer: Absorbs bursts and decouples ingestion from processing, so a slow index never\nrejects incoming data.\n3) Metrics processor: Aggregates and writes numeric series.\n4) Log processor: Parses, enriches, samples, and routes log lines.\n5) Time series store: Compressed numeric points, partitioned by series and time.\n6) Search index: Inverted index over recent logs, which is what makes free-text queries fast.\n7) Object storage: The raw compressed log bodies, cheap and long-lived.\n8) Alert evaluator: Runs rules continuously against recent metrics.\n9) Query service: Fans a user query to whichever store can answer it.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) Ingest tier: Authenticates agents, validates payloads, and enforces per-tenant quotas before anything is accepted.\n2) Kafka buffer: Absorbs bursts and decouples ingestion from processing, so a slow index never rejects incoming data.\n3) Metrics processor: Aggregates and writes numeric series.\n4) Log processor: Parses, enriches, samples, and routes log lines.\n5) Time series store: Compressed numeric points, partitioned by series and time.\n6) Search index: Inverted index over recent logs, which is what makes free-text queries fast.\n7) Object storage: The raw compressed log bodies, cheap and long-lived.\n8) Alert evaluator: Runs rules continuously against recent metrics.\n9) Query service: Fans a user query to whichever store can answer it.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
