      "updated": 1787328238597,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3) Controlling what we keep (SAMPLING, AGGREGATION)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3) Controlling what we keep (SAMPLING, AGGREGATION)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "sg5IZDRYAFXXlOkOOZk5n",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 345,
      "y": 2541.5,
      "width": 999.37548828125,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5f",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 770391002,
      "version": 135,
      "versionNonce": 2104227866,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787328302608,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- JSON LOGGING with consistent fields name\n- Sampling by level: Keep every error and warning, and sample info and debug at some percentage. Most\nlog volume is routine success messages that nobody has ever searched for.\n- Aggregation at the agent: A thousand identical lines become one line with a count. This is\nenormously effective on tight loops and retry storms, which are exactly what produce volume spikes.\n- Tiered retention: Full-fidelity indexed logs for days, then index-free object storage for months,\nthen delete. Each tier is roughly an order of magnitude cheaper than the one above it.\n- Per-tenant quotas: One team turning on debug logging shouldn't degrade observability for everyone\nelse, so quotas belong at the ingest tier where they can reject rather than downstream where the\ndamage is already done.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- JSON LOGGING with consistent fields name\n- Sampling by level: Keep every error and warning, and sample info and debug at some percentage. Most log volume is routine success messages that nobody has ever searched for.\n- Aggregation at the agent: A thousand identical lines become one line with a count. This is enormously effective on tight loops and retry storms, which are exactly what produce volume spikes.\n- Tiered retention: Full-fidelity indexed logs for days, then index-free object storage for months, then delete. Each tier is roughly an order of magnitude cheaper than the one above it.\n- Per-tenant quotas: One team turning on debug logging shouldn't degrade observability for everyone else, so quotas belong at the ingest tier where they can reject rather than downstream where the damage is already done.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "V5RmVs_q-XZ-VRtXCa8t_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 344.9307861328125,
      "y": 2814.94140625,
      "width": 308.41986083984375,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
